				<div class="elementor-column elementor-col-50 elementor-top-column elementor-element elementor-element-c6f1f41" data-id="c6f1f41" data-element_type="column">
			<div class="elementor-widget-wrap elementor-element-populated">
						<section class="elementor-section elementor-inner-section elementor-element elementor-element-e1d77fc elementor-section-boxed elementor-section-height-default elementor-section-height-default" data-id="e1d77fc" data-element_type="section" data-settings="{&quot;background_background&quot;:&quot;classic&quot;}">
						<div class="elementor-container elementor-column-gap-default">
					<div class="elementor-column elementor-col-100 elementor-inner-column elementor-element elementor-element-db5caea" data-id="db5caea" data-element_type="column">
			<div class="elementor-widget-wrap elementor-element-populated">
						<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-9eeb5f1 elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading" data-id="9eeb5f1" data-element_type="widget" data-widget_type="heading.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
					<h6 class="elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default">sometimes your left out to dry.</h6>				</div>
				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-1c1cb47 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor" data-id="1c1cb47" data-element_type="widget" data-widget_type="text-editor.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
									<p>Right now … you probably directly employ staff introduced to you by agencies charging large fees for that priveledge.</p><p>As an employer you have to manage their wages, taxes, holidays as well as rearrange your life to cover their illness, injuries, personal emergencies and when they give notice.</p><p>When they leave … you need to cope with no staff member, organise their replacement, incur agency fees, spend time reviewing and interviewing … and when you finally find someone … you need to train them on your environment, preferences and requirements.</p>								</div>
				</div>
					</div>
		</div>
					</div>
		</section>
					</div>
		</div>
					</div>
		</section>
				<section class="elementor-section elementor-top-section elementor-element elementor-element-1800970 elementor-reverse-mobile elementor-reverse-tablet elementor-section-boxed elementor-section-height-default elementor-section-height-default" data-id="1800970" data-element_type="section" data-settings="{&quot;background_background&quot;:&quot;classic&quot;}">
							<div class="elementor-background-overlay"></div>
							<div class="elementor-container elementor-column-gap-default">
					<div class="elementor-column elementor-col-50 elementor-top-column elementor-element elementor-element-6e120d4" data-id="6e120d4" data-element_type="column">
			<div class="elementor-widget-wrap elementor-element-populated">
						<section class="elementor-section elementor-inner-section elementor-element elementor-element-e689267 elementor-section-boxed elementor-section-height-default elementor-section-height-default" data-id="e689267" data-element_type="section" data-settings="{&quot;background_background&quot;:&quot;classic&quot;}">
						<div class="elementor-container elementor-column-gap-default">
					<div class="elementor-column elementor-col-100 elementor-inner-column elementor-element elementor-element-264d728" data-id="264d728" data-element_type="column">
			<div class="elementor-widget-wrap elementor-element-populated">
						<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-026b3aa elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading" data-id="026b3aa" data-element_type="widget" data-widget_type="heading.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
					<h3 class="elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default">staff as a service means ...</h3>				</div>
				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-98d2f79 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor" data-id="98d2f79" data-element_type="widget" data-widget_type="text-editor.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
									<p>Your not employing an individual and relying solely on them to perform certain duties … your consuming a service that delivers staff to perform those duties and in case of emergencies can easily supply other staff from our team too.</p><p>Let’s imagine your using our service and the nanny we supplied needs to take a few weeks off due to a death in the family. A new nanny from our team, equally skilled and experienced, briefed on the notes the previous nanny made regarding your requirements and preferences, will be with you in hours … with no fees.</p><p>Would that make your life a little easier???</p>								</div>
				</div>
					</div>
		</div>
					</div>
		</section>
					</div>
		</div>
